  "term": "oculomotor changes",
  "definition": "Oculomotor changes are changes in eye-movement behavior during tracking, such as shifts in smooth pursuit, saccade timing, or tracking accuracy. In this source, these changes varied with the target’s motion, the visual context, and whether people were only watching the target or also trying to intercept it by hand.",
